{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "FAO-REC-001, FAO-REC-002, FAO-REC-004, FAO-REC-006, FAO-REC-007: one Per-Asset Reconcile input per policy branch and per bad-input class. Used by test/node/recon.test.mjs against the exported Code node. Thresholds mirror seeds/0006 (scope Spot) in the shape the Get Materiality Thresholds query returns.",
    "special_values": "A value written as {\"$special\": \"undefined\" | \"NaN\" | \"Infinity\" | \"-Infinity\"} stands for that JavaScript value, which JSON cannot carry. The key is kept present on that side.",
    "expect_ratio": "number: inputs.ratio must be a finite number; null: inputs.ratio must be null; any: not checked.",
    "stablecoin_band": "IC-38 (owner decision 2026-11-07): the USDC and USDT ratio_band_upper is 1.05 because stablecoin reserves are held near 105%; floor and band lower stay 1.00. stablecoin_in_band_near_105 sits between the old 1.005 band and 1.05 and is ALLOW; stablecoin_above_band_upper is above 1.05.",
    "thresholds_override": "Optional per case: {\"<asset>\": {<field>: <value>}} replaces those threshold fields for that asset in that case only. The shared thresholds stay equal to seed 0006. Used where a branch is unreachable under the seeded values: the seeded stablecoin floor and band lower are 1.00, so a stablecoin shortfall is BELOW_FLOOR (rule 3) before rule 5 is tested.",
    "stablecoin_usd_materiality": "Owner decision 2026-11-08 (O1): stablecoin USD materiality (rule 5, IN_BAND_USD_MATERIAL) applies to a SHORTFALL only, ledger minus wallet above materiality_usd. A surplus inside the band is governed by the band upper (1.05) alone and ALLOWs. stablecoin_surplus_in_band_above_materiality is the old in_band_usd_material case (the flagship USDT, a 67,890.50 surplus), now ALLOW; stablecoin_kraken_scale_surplus is a 1.04 surplus on a 10,000,000 pool; stablecoin_shortfall_in_band_usd_material keeps rule 5 covered on a shortfall under a threshold override with floor 0.98 and band lower 0.99."
  },
